course: dictionary
lesson: 13249
title: Gherkin and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gherkin is a small cucumber kept in vinegar, so it tastes sharp and sour. Cooks eat it as a pickle. «Dad added two gherkins to his burger.» The word burger tells you a gherkin is food.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «The gherkins sat in a jar on the table.» The jar and the table show you the food meaning. «Visitors took photos of The Gherkin in London.» The capital letters and the city name show you that it is a building.
explain: In the USA and Canada, people often say «pickle» for the same small cucumber. So «I want a pickle on my sandwich» means a gherkin there. Always check the clues around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: A gherkin is a small cucumber kept in vinegar.
fact: Gherkins are grown for pickling, so the cucumber itself is also called a gherkin.
fact: Gherkins often go in burgers, sandwiches and salads.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a gherkin is usually called a «pickle».
fact: «The Gherkin» is an informal nickname for a famous pickle-shaped tower in London.
exercise: «Mia spread butter on her bread and added a gherkin.» What food is a gherkin here? | A slice of cheese | A piece of toast with jam | A bag of crisps | *A small cucumber kept in vinegar
exercise: A sign in a Canadian shop says «Pickles, 2 for 1». What does pickle mean on this sign? | A boat that sails slowly | A word for going to sleep | A sort of bread roll | *A gherkin, a small cucumber kept in vinegar
exercise: «Visitors took photos of The Gherkin in London.» What is The Gherkin? | A river boat | A school for cooks | A kind of sweet biscuit | *A famous pickle-shaped tower
test: «The sandwich had cheese, ham and a sliced gherkin.» What is a gherkin in this sentence? | A bird that sings | A cloud shaped like a fish | Something to wear | *Food, a small cucumber kept in vinegar
test: Ella says that in a Canadian shop, «pickle» means a cucumber kept in vinegar. Is she right? | No, a pickle is a kind of bread | No, a pickle is always a sour sweet | *Yes, in the USA and Canada a pickle is usually a gherkin | No, a pickle is a tower in London
exam: Jamal reads «The gherkins were on the sandwich, but The Gherkin was in London.» What do the capital letters and London show about The Gherkin? | A sweet shop | *A famous pickle-shaped tower in London | A bread roll | A cucumber farm
